A||||2||pontiacs4me||back from the power tour||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||05-15-2001||01:37 AM||||I got back at about 4:45 this morning, we left at about 9am the day before, from kingman AZ.  The day before that we drove from San Bernardino, to Santa Monica beach, to Vegas, 9 hour stay, then to Kingman for the night.  On the way home we saw the meteor crater, and about 400 miles of rain storms.  I averaged about 27 mpg, at 75 mph.  I hit 28 mpg through New Mexico.  <BR>I met Phil and cruised with him for a few legs of the tour.  He is really cool, and his car rocks.  We were pulling out of a gas stop, and he got on it real good, I had my car floored, and all I saw was a little yellow fiero, getting smaller and smaller, out my windshield.  It was really fun though.  There was 1 other fiero on the tour, it was a guy from Oklahoma in a 86 gt.  And I saw a 85 coupe broke down on the side of the road in Arizona somewhere, on the way home.  <BR>In san bernardino, I saw Elanor from gone in 60 seconds.  They also had marylin monroes caddy, and Fords 49 custom.  It was absolutely beautiful.  There were so many awesome cars on the tour, troys orange peel was there, Hotchkis performance had there F-71 camaro there.  Hypertech had there chassis dyno on hand, and they had horsepower competitions every day.   The car that made the most power for the day got an award.  A 1989 mustang LX with a 347 stroker, with blower, nitrous, etc etc made 1140 horse at the rear wheels, and a 1987 grand national with a 231, stroked to like 271 something like that, made 849 horse at the rear wheels.  Thats pretty awesome for a v6.  Anyway, thats about it, I won 3 shirts, and Phil won a Ravin Muffler, in San Bernardino.  But they dont have an application for fieros.  Baer gave away 3 passes to bondurant driving school, and comp cams gave away 2 passes to drive a nascar car at california motor speedway.  GM gave away a 1966 chevy II nova all restored and brand new.  they also gave away 2 crate 355's.  To say the least, it was probably the biggest automotive event to date.  In Kingman, they blocked off 9 city blocks of route 66 for the car show.  The cars lined 66 on both sides, parked side by side, angled and about 2 1/2 feet apart, the lined the side streets, and parking lots.  San Bernardino was even bigger than that.  Hope to see more than 2 other fieros next year.  Hint Hint.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||05-15-2001||07:21 AM||||Welcome Back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||05-15-2001||11:15 AM||||Welcome back, Sounded like you had great fun. I would love to go but $$ is not on my side. I hope to go someday.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
